#: processes/related-work.bpmn:15
#. Diagram label
msgid "Agent"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answers one question: coordinate or not, and how. The question arrives with its context, options and a recommendation, so it can be answered without opening anything (interaction-modality §4.1)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:33
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "beans list --json / beans query over titles AND bodies, open and recently completed. A completed bean is evidence of a decision already made."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:13
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Before new work takes shape, find the work it touches. When a requirement is initiated or updated through a human-agent chat (CRDM), or a method is adopted from a source, search the beans and the repository's issues and open PRs for relevance. Categorize and summarize every hit, then ask the user whether and how to coordinate. Judgement decides the categories and the recommendation; the user decides the coordination. Owner, 2026-09-23 (issue #1023): 'existing beans need to be searched for relevance and categorized (and summarized), same for issues (e.g. github). ask user if they want to coordinate. judgement is used to determine how'. Operating skill: related-work-coordination."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:40
#. Diagram label
msgid "Categorize and summarize"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Coordinate? How?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each hit gets a category (overlaps: coordinate; affected by; out of scope; unrelated) and a one-line summary with its state. Judgement, not a keyword score: say why each is in its category."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:47
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record and act on the answer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Related work known and decided"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:10
#. Diagram label
msgid "Related work: find, sort, summarize, ask to coordinate"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:32
#. Diagram label
msgid "Search beans for relevance"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:36
#. Diagram label
msgid "Search issues and open PRs"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Searches, sorts and summarizes, and recommends. It never links, blocks, merges or comments on another piece of work before the user has answered, because coordinating is a commitment on behalf of the work's owners."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:37
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The repository's issues (open and closed) and its open pull requests. An open PR touching the same files is the collision most worth finding early."
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:25
#. Diagram label
msgid "User"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:31
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work started or changed in chat"
msgstr ""

#: processes/related-work.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write the chosen coordination where it will be found: bean links (--blocked-by, --parent), a line in the issue or PR body, or 'note only'. A declined coordination is recorded too."
msgstr ""
